WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.667 --> 00:00:01.835
-Hey, everybody.

00:00:01.835 --> 00:00:03.169
Welcome to "The Tonight Show"
at-home edition.

00:00:03.169 --> 00:00:06.972
It is me, Jimmy Fallon,
wishing you the best night

00:00:06.972 --> 00:00:08.974
and sleep that you're gonna get
after this 'cause

00:00:08.974 --> 00:00:11.811
usually when I read some jokes,
you doze off, and that's fine.

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:13.813
You're allowed to do that.
You can do whatever you want.

00:00:13.813 --> 00:00:16.549
I'm just here to let you know
that I'm just here.

00:00:16.549 --> 00:00:18.984
That's all. That's what I wanted
to let you know.

00:00:18.984 --> 00:00:21.754
And it's almost Friday,
which basically means

00:00:21.754 --> 00:00:25.091
it's almost Saturday, Sunday,
and Monday is Memorial Day

00:00:25.091 --> 00:00:28.161
and so hopefully some people
get the day off on Monday.

00:00:28.161 --> 00:00:29.596
But thank you so much
for watching.

00:00:29.596 --> 00:00:32.298
Let's get to some jokes here
and some news.

00:00:32.298 --> 00:00:33.766
You guys, it's almost summer
and now

00:00:33.766 --> 00:00:35.368
that more states
are reopening,

00:00:35.368 --> 00:00:38.271
the CDC has released
safety recommendations

00:00:38.271 --> 00:00:41.340
for using public pools.

00:00:41.340 --> 00:00:42.642
Yep, if you haven't seen them,

00:00:42.642 --> 00:00:46.046
it is just a sign that says,
"Eh, I wouldn't."

00:00:48.514 --> 00:00:52.585
You could.
I wouldn't.

00:00:52.585 --> 00:00:55.154
They're also advising people
not to not wear masks

00:00:55.154 --> 00:00:56.956
while in the water.

00:00:56.956 --> 00:00:58.991
I think that's a good call
actually because if you thought

00:00:58.991 --> 00:01:01.094
spotting a Band-Aid floating
in the water was gross,

00:01:01.094 --> 00:01:04.964
imagine a pool filled with
used face masks.

00:01:04.964 --> 00:01:06.732
I think Band-Aids
still freak me out,

00:01:06.732 --> 00:01:12.004
even if it's my Band-Aid.

00:01:12.004 --> 00:01:13.439
I know what's in it.

00:01:13.439 --> 00:01:16.342
Even if it's a little cut
and Neosporin and the Band-Aid,

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:20.013
but if it slips off
and that loop floats towards me,

00:01:20.013 --> 00:01:24.383
it might as well be a shark.

00:01:24.383 --> 00:01:29.088
It's the -- It would honestly
make me not want to swim again.

00:01:29.088 --> 00:01:30.689
Eww!

00:01:30.689 --> 00:01:35.561
What if it's small and there
aren't any children in the pool?

00:01:35.561 --> 00:01:38.063
It's like someone's
pinky toe Band-Aid.

00:01:38.063 --> 00:01:40.566
What? Eww!

00:01:40.566 --> 00:01:42.302
Barf.
Barf.

00:01:42.302 --> 00:01:46.705
Both Johnson &amp; Johnson got sick.

00:01:46.705 --> 00:01:48.641
Today President Trump toured
a Ford

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.710
manufacturing plant in Michigan.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:53.045
He spoke about the coronavirus,
jobs,

00:01:53.045 --> 00:01:57.516
and his plans
to pardon Lori Loughlin.

00:01:57.516 --> 00:02:01.553
"Aunt Becky has been treated
terribly, very terribly."

00:02:01.553 --> 00:02:03.156
That's right.
Everyone is talking about this.

00:02:03.156 --> 00:02:05.758
It came out today that Lori
Loughlin has changed her mind

00:02:05.758 --> 00:02:09.095
and agreed to plead guilty in
the college admission scandal.

00:02:09.095 --> 00:02:10.263
That's right.

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:12.732
Loughlin finally decided to do
what's right

00:02:12.732 --> 00:02:16.235
after a heart-to-heart talk
with Bob Saget.

00:02:16.235 --> 00:02:19.505
"Hey, kiddo.

00:02:19.505 --> 00:02:21.340
You got a second?"

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:25.344
Loughlin will serve two months
in prison, pay a $150,000 fine,

00:02:25.344 --> 00:02:30.884
and this is rough -- she has to
do 100 hours of Hallmark movies.

00:02:30.884 --> 00:02:32.485
I like those movies.
-We love those.

00:02:32.485 --> 00:02:35.889
-I like -- I say like because --

00:02:35.889 --> 00:02:37.457
-Because you actually love.

00:02:37.457 --> 00:02:39.024
-I really do love.

00:02:39.024 --> 00:02:41.293
I love a Hallmark movie.

00:02:41.293 --> 00:02:42.528
I don't even know --

00:02:42.528 --> 00:02:45.364
Have I seen Lori Loughlin
in a Hallmark movie?

00:02:45.364 --> 00:02:48.868
I've seen Candice Cameron.

00:02:48.868 --> 00:02:50.303
I don't know.

00:02:50.303 --> 00:02:52.338
What's my favorite Hallmark one?

00:02:52.338 --> 00:02:54.940
Oh, it's "Single Santa
Seeks Mrs. Claus."

00:02:54.940 --> 00:02:56.342
Steve Guttenberg. Classic.

00:02:56.342 --> 00:02:58.043
Crystal Bernard.
-Crystal Bernard.

00:02:58.043 --> 00:02:59.145
-Oh, I love that one.

00:02:59.145 --> 00:03:02.415
I love Hallmark movies.

00:03:02.415 --> 00:03:05.651
I'm saying it like
I'm the only person

00:03:05.651 --> 00:03:07.086
like it's a bizarre thing.

00:03:07.086 --> 00:03:09.088
Everyone loves Hallmark movies.
Right?

00:03:09.088 --> 00:03:11.691
-I think so.
-I do.

00:03:11.691 --> 00:03:14.426
-I do.

00:03:14.426 --> 00:03:16.862
-Yesterday in Michigan, barbers

00:03:16.862 --> 00:03:18.931
gave haircuts
outside the capitol

00:03:18.931 --> 00:03:23.503
in a new protest
called Operation Haircut.

00:03:23.503 --> 00:03:26.172
Years from now when I look back
at all the great protests

00:03:26.172 --> 00:03:28.240
in our nation's history,

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:30.342
I will always think about
the Boston Tea Party,

00:03:30.342 --> 00:03:31.377
the March on Washington,

00:03:31.377 --> 00:03:35.080
and, of course,
Operation Haircut.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.250
Well, the NBA might try to
resume their season

00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:40.619
by playing all the games
at Disney World.

00:03:40.619 --> 00:03:41.688
Here's how it will work.

00:03:41.688 --> 00:03:43.156
The players wait in line
for three hours

00:03:43.156 --> 00:03:45.891
then the game lasts two minutes.

00:03:45.891 --> 00:03:47.826
A new report found that
canceling college football

00:03:47.826 --> 00:03:52.198
this season would result
in the loss of $4 billion.

00:03:52.198 --> 00:03:53.566
That's crazy.

00:03:53.566 --> 00:03:55.168
That's like taking all the money
college football players

00:03:55.168 --> 00:03:58.204
will make this year
and adding $4 billion.

00:04:00.973 --> 00:04:04.677
Kellogg's is releasing
a Fruit Loops --

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.479
Are we doing this joke?

00:04:06.479 --> 00:04:08.781
Alright.
Kellogg's is releasing

00:04:08.781 --> 00:04:11.551
a Fruit Loops and Frosted Flakes
mashup cereal.

00:04:11.551 --> 00:04:15.121
Yeah, Frosted Flakes
and Fruit Loops in the same box.

00:04:15.121 --> 00:04:17.490
It should be better than
the Honey Nut Cheerios

00:04:17.490 --> 00:04:21.026
Grape Nuts mashup -- Nut-Nuts.

00:04:21.026 --> 00:04:23.396
I would eat that too.

00:04:23.396 --> 00:04:25.131
I love Grape Nuts.

00:04:25.131 --> 00:04:26.832
I don't like soggy Grape Nuts.

00:04:26.832 --> 00:04:30.403
That's up there with Band-Aids.

00:04:30.403 --> 00:04:34.974
However, Grape Nut ice cream?

00:04:34.974 --> 00:04:37.410
We'll have that conversation.

00:04:37.410 --> 00:04:40.212
We'll walk down
that road together.

00:04:40.212 --> 00:04:43.416
Well, a pair of scientists said
that they found 47 traits

00:04:43.416 --> 00:04:45.784
that make flirting effective.

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:47.719
When people said they want
to see the results,

00:04:47.719 --> 00:04:51.224
scientists were like,
"You want to see the results."

00:04:53.692 --> 00:04:56.528
"No, I want to see the results."
"You can see them.

00:04:56.528 --> 00:04:59.498
You can see all the results
if you want.

00:04:59.498 --> 00:05:02.101
Do you want to wear
my lab jacket?

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.736
You don't have to."

00:05:06.439 --> 00:05:07.973
You take the lab jacket off

00:05:07.973 --> 00:05:11.510
and you put it over the person
and they're on the swing set.

00:05:11.510 --> 00:05:16.081
♪ What would you
do if I sang ♪

00:05:16.081 --> 00:05:20.086
Hey, I saw that tomorrow Pacman
turns 40 years old.

00:05:20.086 --> 00:05:22.154
Like a lot of 40-year-olds,
he went in for a checkup

00:05:22.154 --> 00:05:23.388
and his doctor was like,

00:05:23.388 --> 00:05:25.324
"I'm going to need you
to cut back on the dots

00:05:25.324 --> 00:05:27.192
and the ghosts
and stuff like that.

00:05:27.192 --> 00:05:30.563
Can you do that for me?"

00:05:30.563 --> 00:05:35.168
"I'm really only having like one
or two dots a week."

00:05:35.168 --> 00:05:37.770
Okay.

00:05:37.770 --> 00:05:39.639
Finally, this is a great story.
I heard about a runner

00:05:39.639 --> 00:05:42.975
who finished 19 marathons
in 19 days

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.311
to raise money
for coronavirus relief.

00:05:45.311 --> 00:05:47.680
Then tomorrow he's running
a 20th marathon

00:05:47.680 --> 00:05:49.415
to raise money
for his bloody nipples.

00:05:49.415 --> 00:05:52.084
Everybody, that's the monologue
right there.

00:05:52.084 --> 00:05:53.619
Thank you very, very much.

00:05:53.619 --> 00:05:55.755
What a show we have tonight.
You know her.

00:05:55.755 --> 00:05:57.356
You love her.
You can't live without her.

00:05:57.356 --> 00:06:00.492
11 seasons on "Modern Family,"
oh, my goodness.

00:06:00.492 --> 00:06:03.796
Sofia Vergara is on the show,
and now she's a judge

00:06:03.796 --> 00:06:05.698
on "America's Got Talent."

00:06:05.698 --> 00:06:08.134
She probably thought she
was getting a little time off.

00:06:08.134 --> 00:06:09.435
No, no, no.

00:06:09.435 --> 00:06:10.837
Life doesn't work like that.

00:06:10.837 --> 00:06:12.705
We need more Sofia Vergara.

00:06:12.705 --> 00:06:13.873
We love you.

00:06:13.873 --> 00:06:15.975
And now she's doing my show.

00:06:15.975 --> 00:06:19.545
She's raising money for
kiva.org, which is very cool.

00:06:19.545 --> 00:06:21.113
Thank you, Sofia,
for doing the show.

00:06:21.113 --> 00:06:23.982
We also have Steve Coogan
and Rob Brydon,

00:06:23.982 --> 00:06:27.653
two super-funny human beings,
and this is their last --

00:06:27.653 --> 00:06:29.288
I don't know if you have seen
"The Trip,"

00:06:29.288 --> 00:06:30.689
but there is like
three of them now.

00:06:30.689 --> 00:06:34.092
This is the last "Trip" is
coming out tomorrow on demand.

00:06:34.092 --> 00:06:36.995
They go to Greece,
and I cannot wait to watch that.

00:06:36.995 --> 00:06:39.631
It is like having
a conversation at dinner

00:06:39.631 --> 00:06:41.300
with two of
the funniest humans ever.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:45.071
So I'll have a conversation
with them later on Zoom.

00:06:45.071 --> 00:06:46.839
And then to close out the show
music-wise,

00:06:46.839 --> 00:06:50.443
ooh, from Australia,
Courtney Barnett!

00:06:50.443 --> 00:06:52.912
That's my girl.
That's my girl.

00:06:52.912 --> 00:06:56.048
Courtney Barnett.

00:06:56.048 --> 00:06:57.816
I love her, man.

00:06:57.816 --> 00:07:01.453
Hey, tonight we have
a really cool thing.

00:07:01.453 --> 00:07:03.055
I know I'm from New York.

00:07:03.055 --> 00:07:06.659
Born and raised in New York,
but Pizza Hut

00:07:06.659 --> 00:07:08.761
has always kind of been there
for me.

00:07:08.761 --> 00:07:10.796
You know that, honey.
I still order Pizza Hut.

00:07:10.796 --> 00:07:12.565
I love it.
It's hard to find in the city,

00:07:12.565 --> 00:07:15.033
but I find it
and I love it so much.

00:07:15.033 --> 00:07:17.336
And this is a cool thing.

00:07:17.336 --> 00:07:19.939
Actually Pizza Hut is where
I used to go with my parents

00:07:19.939 --> 00:07:21.473
when we had
good nights out like

00:07:21.473 --> 00:07:24.876
if I was celebrating something,

00:07:24.876 --> 00:07:27.513
like even I would say like
graduation or something.

00:07:27.513 --> 00:07:30.049
It was a major deal to go out
to dinner at Pizza Hut.

00:07:30.049 --> 00:07:31.750
Me and my sister
would have a booth.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:32.885
My mom always wanted a booth.

00:07:32.885 --> 00:07:35.153
"Do you have any booths?

00:07:35.153 --> 00:07:37.589
I only want to eat in a booth."

00:07:37.589 --> 00:07:41.093
Okay.
"Yeah. I'm not even hungry."

00:07:41.093 --> 00:07:43.930
Well, a booth opened.
"Okay. We'll take it."

00:07:43.930 --> 00:07:46.899
And they would sit and then
we'd go play Pacman, who's --

00:07:46.899 --> 00:07:50.770
Anyways, Pizza Hut
is doing this cool thing

00:07:50.770 --> 00:07:53.472
because you know what?
They love the graduates,

00:07:53.472 --> 00:07:56.242
and I love the graduates of 2020
and, man,

00:07:56.242 --> 00:07:58.343
you got a raw deal this year.

00:07:58.343 --> 00:07:59.845
No real graduation for you guys

00:07:59.845 --> 00:08:02.214
and no real prom,
and Pizza Hut wanted to,

00:08:02.214 --> 00:08:05.584
I don't know, wanted to make it
a little bit cooler for you.

00:08:05.584 --> 00:08:06.685
So guess what.

00:08:06.685 --> 00:08:10.756
They've giving out
500,000 pizzas

00:08:10.756 --> 00:08:13.859
to graduates of 2020
and their families.

00:08:13.859 --> 00:08:15.293
500,000 pizzas.

00:08:15.293 --> 00:08:20.466
So if you want, go to
pizzahut.com/gradparty,

00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:22.401
and they're going to use

00:08:22.401 --> 00:08:25.371
the contactless curbside pickup
for this.

00:08:25.371 --> 00:08:28.674
So thank you to America's
dairy farmers

00:08:28.674 --> 00:08:31.844
and for Pizza Hut
for doing this cool thing,

00:08:31.844 --> 00:08:34.746
and congratulations,
class of 2020.

00:08:34.746 --> 00:08:38.284
You know we love you.

00:08:38.284 --> 00:08:39.552
That's pretty, pretty cool.

00:08:39.552 --> 00:08:42.321
Oh, you know what?
I forgot to do this.

00:08:42.321 --> 00:08:44.556
Pretend you didn't hear that.

00:08:44.556 --> 00:08:46.758
Hey, guys.

00:08:46.758 --> 00:08:49.761
It's Jimmy Fallon
talking to you.

00:08:49.761 --> 00:08:51.230
This is for the graduates.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.134
So if you are not a graduate of
2020, please leave the room.

00:08:55.134 --> 00:08:59.471
Graduates, this was a tough one.

00:08:59.471 --> 00:09:01.207
You deserve everything.

00:09:01.207 --> 00:09:02.041
And you know what?

00:09:02.041 --> 00:09:03.575
Pizza Hut is there for you.

00:09:03.575 --> 00:09:05.244
They want you
to have everything.

00:09:05.244 --> 00:09:09.248
If you go to
pizzahut.com/gradparty,

00:09:09.248 --> 00:09:11.616
they're going to give -- well,
they're not gonna give you --

00:09:11.616 --> 00:09:13.486
but they're gonna give,
in total,

00:09:13.486 --> 00:09:17.923
500,000 pizzas to you guys
to have a little party

00:09:17.923 --> 00:09:19.257
because you deserve it.

00:09:19.257 --> 00:09:23.396
Thank you, Pizza Hut, and
thank you, graduates of 2020.

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:27.733
♪ Thank you so much ♪

00:09:27.733 --> 00:09:31.069
♪ Thank you ♪

00:09:31.069 --> 00:09:31.871
Alright. Here we go.

